{"id": "EUVD-2026-101039", "enisaUuid": "856462e0-0300-3508-8825-edea1dc38a40", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nx86/amd_node: Avoid divide by zero on virtualized systems\n\nOn a virtualized system, the number of nodes does not have a relationship to\nthe number of roots.  A Xen PVH dom0 can calculate roots_per_node as 0, which\ncrashes with a divide by zero in:\n\n  if (count++ % roots_per_node)\n\nbecause the underlying topology code on Xen ends up making num_nodes\n2 and num_roots 1 and the integer division result is 0.\n\nThe issue is seen with Xen, but it could affect other systems.\n\nSet roots_per_node to 1 in this case. Print a firmware bug when this is\nperformed for non-virtualized systems.\n\n  [ bp: Massage commit message. ]", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:25:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9273a90465d58b82aca4bea71451ef6bee084928", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94e984d8858a3228952b02f84e66610961098cc2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72bd92bd8190d7869ecb462649ca40f297822a33"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98390", "GHSA-fx97-gm68-7q96"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "67d897b8-7542-3e70-ab2b-79cdebcc71b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "7b11519f-a265-3dc6-b63f-104d13e6379a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "84d9a38b-017c-3fd1-933f-ece925ddf0c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4b61d9c2e496b5f0a10e29e355a1465c8738bb <72bd92bd8190d7869ecb462649ca40f297822a33"}, {"id": "9738e3a8-10eb-30b1-a19b-0d0a252fee43", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4b61d9c2e496b5f0a10e29e355a1465c8738bb <94e984d8858a3228952b02f84e66610961098cc2"}, {"id": "9e0a877d-765c-3dc4-9ba6-0b101ea84758", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "a59a8783-3397-3f66-ace7-0694108e5865", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4ad899a33198ab6335732c769835d035e66894a"}, {"id": "a7808ba6-6def-3524-8838-64fcb3e25a08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b172258e-d795-3802-a24e-3a0c97db30ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0a4b61d9c2e496b5f0a10e29e355a1465c8738bb <9273a90465d58b82aca4bea71451ef6bee084928"}, {"id": "c4a065b7-f5d9-3f65-8c46-77163636e262", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "e2eecfb1-8c7f-3c28-bd1f-0d999548bcc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17.8 <6.18"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7feca990-c059-3b35-b95e-474147807e41", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}